  {
    "id": "fn.concat-at-limit",
    "description": "LEN(CONCAT(REPT(\"a\", 32767))) is 32767 (exactly the UTF-16 cap for ASCII). Microsoft says 32767 characters; that is the cell-width cap, not Compat-v2 LEN scalars.",
    "tags": [
      "concat",
      "text"
    ],
    "formula": "=LEN(CONCAT(REPT(\"a\", 32767)))",
    "expected": {
      "number": 32767
    }
  },
